# REAL operating-mode layer. Apply drone -> this file -> mission.parm.
# Intentionally no parameter entries yet: real sensor limits and clearance are
# hardware properties in config/ardupilot/drones/x500.parm (0.15 m, 12 m, 0.17 m).
# Preserve the installed hardware backend; the user's sensor type/interface is
# not known, so do not invent RNGFND1_TYPE. The verified uploader checks that it
# is enabled and not the SITL backend before applying rangefinder parameters.
# Do not copy SIM_*, native SITL backend 100, zero minimum/clearance, no-RC
# failsafe suppression, or simulator navigation shortcuts into a REAL stack.
# Empty or omitted mode files are supported. Add future hardware-independent
# REAL mode settings here only after individual review, with units and safety
# rationale. This file is not evidence of active sensor health or flight safety.
# REAL upload is explicitly invoked with --upload-params before MOOS starts,
# checks fresh native ground/disarm throughout, and verifies final FC readback.
# It does not arm/change mode/reboot/reset estimators. Required reboot changes
# stop launch pending operator intervention; there is no automatic rollback.
# https://ardupilot.org/dev/docs/mavlink-get-set-params.html

# REAL precision-camera mounting placeholders: deliberately COMMENTED OUT.
# No physical offsets were supplied; do not copy SITL's zero assumptions.
# Before activating any entry, survey the camera optical center relative to
# the vehicle body origin used by ArduPilot/observation producer. Use body FRD
# axes (forward/right/down), signed METRES, not centimetres or GPS-antenna/deck
# coordinates. Upstream per-axis documented range -5..5 m, increments 0.01 m.
# Validate whether the producer supplies camera-origin or already translated
# vehicle-origin observations: axes and origin are distinct, and incorrect
# duplicate/missing compensation biases native landing geometry. These fields
# do not configure yaw/rotation, desired landing offsets or rangefinder mounting.
# Once individually reviewed, hardware-specific values should live in the
# per-drone profile for reuse; an active REAL-mode entry would override it.
# Leaving these commented preserves existing FC values, not necessarily zero.
# Neither a placeholder nor eventual readback proves mounting correctness,
# sensor health, target acquisition or safe touchdown. No flight command or
# custom patch is added. Source: libraries/AC_PrecLand/AC_PrecLand.cpp,
# var_info/construct_pos_meas/run_output_prediction, reviewed Copter 4.7.1.

# PLND_CAM_POS_X -- measured forward offset, metres; positive ahead of body
# origin, negative behind. Placeholder is not a selected value. Replace with
# a surveyed signed number only after validating the producer's origin handling.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#plnd-cam-pos-x
# PLND_CAM_POS_X <MEASURED_FORWARD_M>

# PLND_CAM_POS_Y -- measured right offset, metres; positive right, negative
# left of body origin. No lateral mounting value is known or being uploaded;
# this is not target-relative horizontal error or PEARL's lateral separation.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#plnd-cam-pos-y
# PLND_CAM_POS_Y <MEASURED_RIGHT_M>

# PLND_CAM_POS_Z -- measured down offset, metres; positive below body origin,
# negative above. This is not grounded sensor clearance, Home/MSL altitude or
# target distance. Do not substitute the rangefinder's 0.17 m ground clearance.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#plnd-cam-pos-z
# PLND_CAM_POS_Z <MEASURED_DOWN_M>

# REAL desired landing offsets: deliberately COMMENTED OUT, no values selected.
# These are signed CENTIMETRES (-20..20 cm documented, increments 1 cm), not
# metre-valued mounting offsets. Establish the desired camera-to-target landing
# displacement from aircraft/deck geometry and validate it before activating.
# Do not use these to conceal wrong observation/mount geometry. The camera,
# gear footprint and clearance objective may differ; centered camera placement
# alone is not proof of safe physical recovery. Confirm the frame convention.
# Native run_output_prediction rotates body-frame offsets using aircraft
# attitude, not platform heading, and shifts the landing estimate used for
# guidance, the XY descent gate and remembered-target retry point. Camera
# mounting compensation remains separate. Nonzero choices can therefore
# deliberately move the landing objective and change retry positioning.
# Leaving placeholders commented preserves current FC values, not necessarily
# zero; shared mission entries do not override them. Readback alone cannot prove
# suitable deck clearance, mounting correctness, sensor health or touchdown.
# No flight/RTL command or custom firmware patch is added by this documentation.
# Source: libraries/AC_PrecLand/AC_PrecLand.cpp, var_info/run_output_prediction,
# reviewed companion Copter 4.7.1.

# PLND_LAND_OFS_X -- desired camera landing displacement forward of target,
# cm, in vehicle body frame (positive forward, negative aft). Replace the
# placeholder with an individually reviewed signed number, not the measured
# camera-to-vehicle mount distance. A guessed value can bias the landing point.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#plnd-land-ofs-x
# PLND_LAND_OFS_X <DESIRED_FORWARD_CM>

# PLND_LAND_OFS_Y -- desired camera landing displacement right of target,
# cm, in vehicle body frame (positive right, negative left). Select after
# checking the intended gear/deck footprint and aircraft yaw; no real lateral
# offset has been approved or is being uploaded by this commented placeholder.
# https://ardupilot.org/copter/docs/parameters.html#plnd-land-ofs-y
# PLND_LAND_OFS_Y <DESIRED_RIGHT_CM>
